QCD -Quantum Chromodynamics 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote
Chapther 5 in Grossman
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Quantum ChromoDynamics (QCD),
 the theory of strong interactions,
 is our first example of a
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
non-Abelian theory.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
QCD is a local 
\begin_inset Formula $SU\left(3\right)_{c}$
\end_inset

(c for color) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This theory has 6 left handed and six right-handed fermions fields,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
Q_{Li}\left(3\right),\qquad Q_{Ri}\left(3\right),\qquad i=1,\ldots,6.
\end{equation}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
there are no scalars.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
The Lagrangian
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We impose 
\begin_inset Formula $SU\left(3\right)_{c}$
\end_inset

 so we need to include a gaude field in the adjoint representation of 
\begin_inset Formula $SU\left(3\right)_{c},G^{\mu}_{a}$
\end_inset

 .
 that we call the gluon field.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The gluon field strength is given by
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
G^{\mu\nu}_{a}=\partial^{\mu}G^{\nu}_{a}-\partial^{\nu}G^{\mu}_{a}-g_{s}f_{abc}G^{\mu}_{b}G^{\nu}_{c}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Where 
\begin_inset Formula $L_{a}a=1,\ldots8$
\end_inset

 are the generators of 
\begin_inset Formula $SU\left(3\right)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\left[L_{a},L_{b}\right]=if_{abc}L_{c}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

